-- coa17-part21a-ch5.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21A, Chapter 5 -- Protection from disclosure (ss 790ZF
-- to 790ZH; lines 10723-10756 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Chapters 3 and 4 (ss 790M to 790ZE, lines 10681-10722) are blank in
-- this text (each section shows only a row of dots): they have coverage rows in NOTES.md and no L4. LAYER 1: the law,
-- objectively. SOURCE, TARGET and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER are as in coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE: the text says yes; JUST
-- FALSE: the text says no in its own words; NOTHING: the text does not decide; a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- SEAMS. `s 1121 the officer is in default` (coa24); ss 240 to 244 (coa5) are the rules the information is sent to.
-- NOT ENCODED HERE (machinery, inert reason 2 in NOTES.md): s 790ZG(1), (4), (5), (6), the Secretary of State's power to make
-- regulations protecting material. Subsections (2), (3) and (7) of s 790ZG are encoded because they say who is protected.

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F8 at s 790ZF(2).

§ `Part 21A Chapter 5: Protection from disclosure`

§§ `Protection of information as to usual residential address (s 790ZF)`

-- src:10726 | (2) The information within this subsection is—
-- src:10727 | (a) information as to the usual residential address of a person with significant control over a company, and
-- src:10728 | (b) the information that such a person's service address is his or her usual residential address.
@ref s 790ZF(2) The information within this subsection is (src:10726-10728)
GIVEN `the information is information as to the usual residential address of a person with significant control over a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is the information that such a person's service address is his or her usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZF(2) the information is within this subsection` MEANS
    IF    `the information is information as to the usual residential address of a person with significant control over a company`
       OR `the information is the information that such a person's service address is his or her usual residential address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information within this subsection is— (a) ... (b) ..." (a list closed by "is", not "only": fork F8)

-- src:10725 | (1) The provisions of sections 240 to 244 (directors' residential addresses: protection from disclosure) apply to information within subsection (2) as to protected information within the meaning of those sections.
@ref s 790ZF(1) The provisions of sections 240 to 244 apply to information within subsection (2) as protected information (src:10725)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790ZF(2) for the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZF(1) sections 240 to 244 apply to the information as protected information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 790ZF(2) for the information`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to information within subsection (2)"

§§ `Power to make regulations protecting material (s 790ZG)`

-- src:10734 | (2) “Relevant PSC particulars” means such particulars of a person with significant control over the company as may be prescribed.
@ref s 790ZG(2) "Relevant PSC particulars" means such particulars of a person with significant control as may be prescribed (src:10734)
GIVEN `the particulars are of a kind prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZG(2) the particulars are relevant PSC particulars` MEANS
    IF `the particulars are of a kind prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant PSC particulars” means such particulars of a person with significant control over the company as may be prescribed."

-- src:10735 | (3) The reference in subsection (2) to a person with significant control over the company—
-- src:10736 | (a) includes a person who used to be such a person, but
-- src:10737 | (b) does not include any person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12) as if the person were an individual.
@ref s 790ZG(3) The reference in subsection (2) to a person with significant control (src:10735-10737)
GIVEN `the person used to be a person with significant control over the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12) as if the person were an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZG(3) the person counts as a person with significant control over the company for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12) as if the person were an individual`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include any person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12) as if the person were an individual"
    ELSE IF `the person used to be a person with significant control over the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a person who used to be such a person"; a current person with significant control is not dealt with here

-- src:10749 | (7) Nothing in this section or in regulations made under it affects the use or disclosure of particulars of a person in any other capacity (for example, the use or disclosure of particulars of a person in that person‘s capacity as a member or director of the company).
@ref s 790ZG(7) Nothing in this section or in regulations made under it affects the use or disclosure of particulars of a person in any other capacity (src:10749)
GIVEN `the particulars are of a person in another capacity (for example as a member or director of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZG(7) this section or regulations under it affect the use or disclosure of the particulars` MEANS
    IF `the particulars are of a person in another capacity (for example as a member or director of the company)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or in regulations made under it affects the use or disclosure of particulars of a person in any other capacity"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "particulars of a person in any other capacity"

§§ `Offence of failing to comply with regulations under section 790ZG (s 790ZH)`

-- src:10751 | (1) If a company contravenes a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by virtue of regulations under subsection 790ZG, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10752 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10753 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 790ZH(1) If a company contravenes a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by virtue of regulations under section 790ZG (src:10751-10753)
GIVEN `the company contravenes a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by virtue of regulations under section 790ZG` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZH(1)(a) an offence is committed by the company` MEANS
    IF `the company contravenes a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by virtue of regulations under section 790ZG`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by virtue of regulations under subsection 790ZG" (the if fails)

@ref s 790ZH(1)(b) every officer of the company who is in default (src:10751-10753)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790ZH(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790ZH(1)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the answer under section 790ZH(1)(a)` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:10754 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:10755 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:10756 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 790ZH(2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction (src:10754-10756)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 790ZH(2) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 0.1)
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 0.1)
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on summary conviction— (a) in England and Wales, to a fine; (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5"
